\f0\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf3 \strokec3 WHAT CHANGED\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sl403\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \AppleTypeServices \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The PDF/print export no longer builds a document by interpolating RAMS data into an HTML string.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The export now opens a print window and constructs the document using DOM nodes and 
\f2 \cb4 textContent
\f1 \cb1 .\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Risk labels are normalised to known CSS classes before being applied.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Generated text, user-entered text, and AI-returned content are treated as text, not executable markup.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl403\sa215\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf3 \strokec3 WHY IT MATTERS\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl403\sa260\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \AppleTypeServices \cf2 \strokec2 The previous implementation used 
\f2 \cb4 document.write
\f1 \cb1  with generated RAMS fields embedded directly in HTML. If a generated value contained HTML-like content, it could alter the exported document structure. The new path avoids that by assigning all RAMS content through text nodes. \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl403\sa215\partightenfactor0

